<title>USA: Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</title>
<headline>Leslie-ADM soybean production survey by state.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tables contain state-by-state soybean production estimates published in the Leslie-ADM Investor Services Crop survey.</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION (IN 000'S BUSHELS)</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 9/1/96  USDA 8/1/96   USDA 1995</p>
<p> PENN	   12,825	 12,540	 9,450</p>
<p> OHIO	  148,170	157,150     153,140</p>
<p> INDIANA     176,880	187,600     194,220</p>
<p> ILLINOIS    364,450	374,300     373,450</p>
<p> MICHIGAN     49,200	 55,760	59,600</p>
<p> WISCONSIN    33,060	 35,670	34,400</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 9/1/96  USDA 8/1/96   USDA 1995</p>
<p> MINN	  224,200	224,200     232,000</p>
<p> IOWA	  406,350	425,250     398,180</p>
<p> MISSOURI    137,700	137,700     130,500</p>
<p> N DAKOTA     22,960	 24,600	18,560</p>
<p> S DAKOTA     78,175	 84,800	75,000</p>
<p> NEBRASKA    126,420	126,420	99,450</p>
<p> KANSAS	 65,000	 60,000	51,250</p>
<p> MARYLAND     15,360	 15,840	11,730</p>
<p> VIRGINIA     16,320	 15,360	11,280</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 9/1/96  USDA 8/1/96   USDA 1995</p>
<p> N CAROLINA   40,200	 37,200	26,750</p>
<p> S CAROLINA   15,120	 13,500	12,720</p>
<p> GEORGIA	12,090	 10,140	 8,370</p>
<p> KENTUCKY     42,480	 42,480	41,400</p>
<p> TENNESSEE    35,650	 36,800	34,560</p>
<p> ALABAMA	 9,135	  8,820	 5,400</p>
<p> MISS	   49,000	 47,250	37,800</p>
<p> ARKANSAS    104,400	108,000	86,700</p>
<p>U.S. SOYBEAN PRODUCTION</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 9/1/96  USDA 8/1/96   USDA 1995</p>
